    {
      "name": "asset_purpose_signal",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.25,
      "source_groundedness": 0.5,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Mapping a Dell laptop to 'office_equipment' or AWS to 'server_infrastructure' is a warranted inference, but 'purpose' is not stated in the source text and largely restates asset_category_type (hardware->office_equipment near-deterministically), so it adds little independent signal and asserts purpose the text is silent on."
    },
    {
      "name": "expense_source_indicator",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.5,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Cleanly extracted from short_description phrasing ('Procurement of' -> procurement, 'Automated creation' -> automated_creation). This 'how the record originated' axis is plausibly predictive of decline behaviour and is well grounded."
    },
    {
      "name": "departmental_context",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.3,
      "source_groundedness": 0.2,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "An original 'department' column already exists, making this largely redundant. More critically, none of the sampled source texts contain department info, yet confident values (customer_support, sales) are asserted for rows whose text is silent on department -- unsupported specifics."
    },
    {
      "name": "source_system_origin",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.4,
      "source_groundedness": 0.3,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Every sampled row is labelled 'internal_ticket_system' regardless of content (including an asset-management-style 'Automated creation' entry), and the source text gives no explicit originating system. Overlaps with the original source_id/type columns and the specific system is invented rather than read from text."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.35,
  "source_groundedness": 0.5,
  "rationale": "The columns are asset-inventory categorisations that only weakly serve a query about what predicts travel-expense declines; expense_source_indicator is the most useful and best-grounded, while asset_purpose_signal is largely a restatement of asset_category_type. Groundedness is uneven: extraction-based columns (category, source_indicator) read the text soundly, but departmental_context and source_system_origin assert specifics (department, originating system) not present in the sampled source text and partly duplicate existing original columns."
